  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposal, by reason of insufficient gross internal floor area (GIA) would create a cramped and poor standard of living accommodation for future occupiers to the detriment of their residential amenity, contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2021), Policy D6 of The London Plan (2021), Policy CS1 K of the Harrow Core Strategy (2013), policies DM1 and DM26 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013), the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide Supplementary Planning Document (2010).",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposal, by reason of inappropriate ground floor frontage, which includes combined waste and cycle storage and loss of commercial floorspace within a Neighbourhood Centre would be detrimental to the character, function, vitality and viability of the neighbourhood centre, and by reason of no alternative location for the refuse and cycle storage for the intended residential development, would be detrimental to the amenity of future occupiers and would restrict the uptake of sustainable modes of transportation contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2021); Policy SD8 and T5 of The London Plan (2021); Policy CS1B of the Harrow Core Strategy (2013) and  policies DM1, DM2, DM26, DM38, DM42 and DM45 of Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013).",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposed rear dormers, by reason of poor design, excessive bulk and inadequate visual containment within the existing roof form and when viewed together with the existing two storey rear extension, would result in  a contrived and incongruous addition that would unacceptably harm the character and appearance of the original building and the visual amenities of the area, contrary to policies D3 (D(1) and D(11)) of The London Plan (2021), Policy CS1.B of the Harrow Core Strategy (2012), Policy DM1 of the Development Management Local Plans Policies (2013) and  Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010)."
  ],
